meta {
  name: Day
  type: http
  seq: 14
}

get {
  url: {{api}}/bonds/{{bondId}}/days/{{date}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  If-None-Match: {{dayETag}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) bru.setVar("dayETag", res.getHeader("etag"));
}

docs {
  One day of the archive: the same object Days lists. Run Days first, which keeps the date; or set date yourself, as YYYY-MM-DD. A date that is not in your archive is 404 DAY_NOT_FOUND, whatever the reason.

  Send it twice. The first answer is 200 with an ETag, which is kept; the second sends it back as If-None-Match and is 304 with no body, because nothing you would be shown has changed. Mark or unmark an entry of that day and it is 200 again, under a new ETag. Your partner's marks never change it: they are not in what you are sent. (Days answers If-None-Match the same way.)

  Before the first send dayETag is not set, and the header goes out as written, which matches nothing: 200.
}
